<DocsLayout
  title="Credentials — Overview"
  description="Issue, hold, and verify W3C Verifiable Credentials with the Attestto VC SDK. Ed25519 and ES256 cryptography, zero native dependencies."
  currentPath="/docs/credentials/"
>
  <h1>Credentials</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Issue, hold, and verify W3C Verifiable Credentials with a pure JavaScript SDK.
    No native dependencies, no server required.
  </p>

  <h2>The credential lifecycle</h2>
  <p>
    Every credential follows three stages: <strong>Issue</strong>,
    <strong>Hold</strong>, and <strong>Verify</strong>.
  </p>

  <ol style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Issue</strong> — An issuer signs claims about a subject, producing a Verifiable Credential.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Hold</strong> — The subject stores the credential in a wallet or vault.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Verify</strong> — A verifier checks the signature, expiration, issuer, and optional revocation status.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>The SDK</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>@attestto-com/vc-sdk</code> package implements the full lifecycle.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock lang="Terminal">
<Fragment set:html={`npm install <span class="c-str">@attestto-com/vc-sdk</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h3>Highlights</h3>
  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">W3C VC Data Model v2.0</strong> — fully compliant credential structure and JSON-LD contexts.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Zero native dependencies</strong> — pure JavaScript cryptography via <code>@noble/curves</code>. Works in Node.js, Deno, Bun, and the browser.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Ed25519 + ES256</strong> — two signature algorithms out of the box.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">Pluggable schema system</strong> — extend with domain-specific credential types and JSON-LD contexts.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">DID-agnostic</strong> — works with any DID method (did:web, did:sns, did:key, did:pki).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Quick example</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="overview.ts">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> VCIssuer, VCVerifier, generateKeyPair <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-cm">// Generate keys and issue a credential</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> keys = <span class="c-fn">generateKeyPair</span>()
<span class="c-kw">const</span> issuer = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCIssuer</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span> did: <span class="c-str">'did:web:example.com'</span>, privateKey: keys.privateKey <span class="c-br">}</span>)

<span class="c-kw">const</span> vc = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-str">'ProfessionalLicense'</span>,
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:holder.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span> license: <span class="c-str">'Engineering'</span>, number: <span class="c-str">'ENG-2026-001'</span> <span class="c-br">}</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

<span class="c-cm">// Verify it</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> verifier = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCVerifier</span>()
<span class="c-kw">const</span> result = <span class="c-kw">await</span> verifier.<span class="c-fn">verifyWithKey</span>(vc, keys.publicKey, <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span>)
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(result.valid) <span class="c-cm">// true</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="info">
    <strong>No server needed.</strong> The SDK runs entirely client-side. Keys are generated
    in-process and credentials are self-contained — no API calls, no blockchain writes required
    for basic issuance and verification.
  </Callout>

